                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                        "entry_id": "ba4bb57b-17aa-3b44-8360-e1038b678681",
                        "glosses": [
                            "текст. ткань с шёлковой основой и вытканным на ней золотым или серебряным узором"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20b585c7-b9f3-4d9e-a129-d6982ae94f2f",
                                "sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                                "text": "Вот вам и убыток, по меньшей мере рублей на десять, так как гроб пришлось бы делать дорогой, с глазетом."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c4af074-0370-4838-8662-824695bda696",
                                "sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                                "text": "Вдоль стен расставлены были стулья и диванчики, другой мебели в сионской горнице не было, кроме стола в переднем углу, накрытого чистой скатертью из гладкого серебряного глазета."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ab86168-8222-406b-bc72-fb1ec2ab4fcb",
                                "sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                                "text": "Вельможа, одетый с ног до головы во французский глазет и убранный по последней парижской моде, защищал пользы отечества и выхвалял любовь к оному…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ea88fc2-3e62-423e-a830-d0e001cbc963",
                                "sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                                "text": "Против ихнего глазету ни одна фирма, даже в самой Твери, выстоять не могла, туды ее в качель."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84701696-c054-4250-bc6d-84b74d4a3fac",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba4bb57b-17aa-3b44-8360-e1038b678681",
                        "source_sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                        "target_lang_word": "brocade",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brocade",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b555d967-00dd-3445-bc30-96f711e68d76",
                                        "entry_id": "ffa36f19-e540-39c8-904f-bf91baeedc94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thick heavy fabric into which raised patterns have been woven, originally in gold and silver; more recently any cloth incorporating raised, woven patterns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "529755d1-23f3-4d00-9903-bfb245594203",
                                                "sense_id": "b555d967-00dd-3445-bc30-96f711e68d76",
                                                "text": "Madame Legarde, the \"glass of fashion and the nurse of form,\" (alias the most fashionable of milliners,) has comfortably assured me, \"that my figure has great merit, and only requires cultivation:\" this is to be done by tissues, brocades, and laces, which are now scattered round me in charming confusion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97605c88-c2fe-4672-98a5-ed6ccd9e6806",
                                                "sense_id": "b555d967-00dd-3445-bc30-96f711e68d76",
                                                "text": "… his desire to stand in brocade and sing Rhadames in Aida was like my eagerness to go far, far beyond fellow intellectuals of my generation who had lost the imaginative soul."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bec5f5f-08e6-4586-95a4-240292b116ed",
                                                "sense_id": "b555d967-00dd-3445-bc30-96f711e68d76",
                                                "text": "I selected a pair of loose, dark trousers bound at the waist with a russet sash, a tunic with an open neck and large pockets, and a cloak of the true fuligin of that guild of which I am still officially a master, lined with particolored brocade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee6194ff-f877-390f-a93b-36d712eb74e0",
                                        "entry_id": "ffa36f19-e540-39c8-904f-bf91baeedc94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An item decorated with brocade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1556e8d2-af91-3818-9109-ca001f2382b2",
                                        "entry_id": "ffa36f19-e540-39c8-904f-bf91baeedc94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several species of noctuid moths such as some species in the genera Calophasia and Hadena"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00f52374-0c2f-46a3-b614-107ace2cb75b",
                                                "sense_id": "1556e8d2-af91-3818-9109-ca001f2382b2",
                                                "text": "Other species considered occasional migrants have become established in the UK in recent years, such as the ... sombre brocade, Blair's mocha, Flame brocade, and Clifden nonpareil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0993c0c4-9145-3e0e-b0d6-4b80e042ed96",
                                        "entry_id": "ffa36f19-e540-39c8-904f-bf91baeedc94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A decorative pattern."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7868850d-41f9-43dc-a4ff-a06bed92d3b6",
                                                "sense_id": "0993c0c4-9145-3e0e-b0d6-4b80e042ed96",
                                                "text": "The shrubbery around the cottages is a brocade of lawns and shrubs intermixed, in fancy patterns, with gravel walks, in various directions, which wind into the woods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23f33700-7a9d-45eb-8df4-e041adbc10fe",
                                                "sense_id": "0993c0c4-9145-3e0e-b0d6-4b80e042ed96",
                                                "text": "It is as though the poets and mystics were weaving a colorful brocade of words with the intention to please God and to show His greatness to the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b439982-ecb0-45fd-88ad-2c0aad471d96",
                                                "sense_id": "0993c0c4-9145-3e0e-b0d6-4b80e042ed96",
                                                "text": "Saying this, Rikyu stepped into the garden, shook a tree and scattered over the garden gold and crimson leaves, scraps of the brocade of autumn!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "brocade",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ec3519e-8816-3eba-8170-2362410f35b9",
                                        "entry_id": "e3be1054-5266-38a1-8a66-1d794fa99196",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To decorate fabric with raised woven patterns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66a52de7-42f6-4ace-a216-0689693aaea5",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba4bb57b-17aa-3b44-8360-e1038b678681",
                        "source_sense_id": "cdf3efd6-8a53-3b84-9ba7-29a9fa2af568",
                        "target_lang_word": "brocart",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brocart",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                        "entry_id": "20f2d2e0-af0e-31a0-b438-ad3e8b043730",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Étoffe de soie brochée d’or ou d’argent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39914e6c-b80b-46b7-9780-cc0c335736d9",
                                                "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                                "text": "[…] un lit de parade, orné d’une infinité de dorures et de rideaux de brocart avec des galons et des franges d’or et d’argent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b224e16-d774-468b-bb75-4ca282f511c8",
                                                "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                                "text": "Son costume, approprié à sa physionomie, était d’une extrême magnificence ; il consistait en une robe de brocart d’or et d’argent et en un manteau de velours nacarat, doublé de menu vair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f133fbb7-1c2c-4764-af1a-b982e9c119a7",
                                                "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                                "text": "Le vieillard semblait plier sous le poids de la chape de brocart, dont les plis somptueux se cassaient derrière lui."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cfb8d2c-fd94-4202-a9f6-5b0e68dda478",
                                                "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                                "text": "Ses petits pieds s’agitaient dans leurs souliers de brocart cerise et argent et menaçaient l’équilibre d’une tasse en pur Wedgwood, tangente à sa cheville nerveuse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7472ac88-2e45-4fe4-8986-225804b06114",
                                                "sense_id": "22831891-4d3e-3210-80af-743e51dc59d7",
                                                "text": "Il y avait dans la cuisine des fauteuils recouverts d’un brocart étranger, et les rideaux de la fenêtre étaient de la même étoffe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
